vanessa bryant says the nike shoes she  designed to honor her late husband and  daughter  kobe and gianna bryant have been leaked  and she's fuming over it insisting they  never should have been made  in the first place on thursday the 39  year old took to instagram posting  a lengthy message explaining that she  recently helped create a version of the  kobe 6 pro tro  that was intended to honor her late  husband and 13 year old daughter  who tragically died in a 2020 helicopter  crash  vanessa says the shoes she designed are  black and white  feature gianna's number two and have  other markings like a butterfly  wings and a halo the problem vanessa  parted ways with nike in the spring and  says she  never gave approval for the shoes to be  made and now  after seeing unverified images online  she claims they've been made  and leaked anyway posting this pic of  someone holding the shoe  in their hand in her statement posted to  instagram  vanessa explains quote nike has not sent  any of these pairs to me and my girls  i do not know how someone else has their  hands on shoes i designed in honor of my  daughter gigi  and we don't i hope these shoes did not  get sold  vanessa adds that she wanted the shoes  to be sold to honor her daughter with  all of the proceeds benefiting the mamba  and mambasita sports foundation  and an unverified instagram user who  originally posted photos of the  mambasita shoes nearly three weeks ago  claims nike is responsible for the shoe  leak  on thursday the unverified user posted a  statement to their insta story alleging  quote  i just want to make it clear that i  don't own a pair of those mambasita  kobes  the pictures i posted are official  product pictures from a nike authorized  retailer  the user continued writing unfortunately  for vanessa bryant  nike clearly sent pairs to this retailer  as well as others with the intent of  selling pairs  et has reached out to nike for comment  but it appears vanessa got more answers  she later responded to a fan's comment  claiming that nike told her the shoes  were in fact  made after she saw them posted online  but she says they were never supposed to  be sold adding quote  we were discussing releasing them after  all but the only way i will agree  is if hundred percent of all of the  proceeds  goes to mamba and mambasita sports so  that kobe and gianna's foundation is the  only entity that benefits from selling  gigi's mambasita shoes  you
 

